            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0264" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1013: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Belt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-27T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1919,
                                1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your March 11, 3 p.m., confidential.</p>
                <p>Elizalde admits that he promised in the name of his Government to pay $859,740
                    but states that his Government misunderstood him as he used the word coupon in
                    the singular form believing that only one coupon was paid annually whereas in
                    fact two are paid. He has promised to telegraph his Government urging the
                    payment of the full amount as promised Department and states that he hopes that
                    he will be able to arrange the matter if there is sufficient money in the
                    Ecuadorian Treasury. Endeavor to ascertain and cable Department whether Ecuador
                    is in a position to make the remaining payment on the $859,740.</p>
                <p>Talk this matter over informally with Norton and cable his opinion as to whether
                    the full payment should be pressed for, but do not take matter up with
                    Ecuadorean Govt. without Department’s instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
